data.text:
There's already `[data-component=reasoning-part][data-auto-collapse]` - let me get that full rule. The user wants inline reasoning hidden from the middle of the transcript, and only shown at the botto...Yes, that should work perfectly. The hot-reload CSS is already active, so we can test it live.

Here’s the clean rule that hides every inline reasoning-part from the message list (so nothing ever appears in the middle of the transcript), while still letting the bottom-right dock show during streaming:

```css
 .message-list [data-component="reasoning-part"],
  .vscode-session-turn [data-component="reasoning-part"] {
    display: none !important;
  }
```

That single rule does exactly what you want:  
- Old reasoning stays collapsed in the history (or hidden if you prefer).

