data.text:
The user says they stopped seeing the reasoning window entirely. This is likely because of the CSS I added that hides reasoning-part in the transcript:
I see the issue now. The CSS is too aggressive and is hiding the entire session-dock (working-indicator) because it matches the `:has(> [data-component="reasoning-part"])` selector on `.vscode-session-turn`.

The dock is a parent container that contains reasoning-part, so it gets hidden too.

 To fix this, we need to be more specific about which reasoning-part we want to hide:

- Only hide reasoning-part that are **inside** message turns (the inline ones during tool calls)
- Keep the ones that are **direct children** of the session-dock (the live streaming ones at the bottom)

Here's the updated CSS:

```css
/* Hide inline reasoning during tool calls (in the middle of messages) */
.message-list [data-component="reasoning-part"]:not([data-streaming]) {
  display: none !important;
}

/* Keep streaming reasoning at the bottom dock */
.vscode-session-turn [data-component=" reasoning-part"][data-streaming],
.message-list [data-component="reasoning-part"][data-streaming] {
  display: block !important;
  position: sticky !important;
  bottom: 0 !important;
  z-index: 20 !important;
  background: var(--background-base) !important;
 border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
}
```

This should:
- Hide completed reasoning that's embedded in the middle of tool calls
- Keep the live streaming reasoning visible at the bottom dock
- Not affect the working-indicator structure

The key is the `:not([data-streaming])` on the message-list selector - this targets only the inline ones, not the dock ones.

Also remove the broad `:has()` selector entirely since it's causing the dock to disappear.

