data.text:
The user is showing screenshots of the Kilo chat markdown. They're saying line gaps and paragraph gaps are still too much - not optimized for UX readability.
I see the issue—those gaps are definitely too loose for a clean, scannable read. The double-margin problem on adjacent paragraphs is a classic trap, and the heading margins are probably stacking too much vertical space.

Let me tighten it up:

- Drop paragraph bottom margin to 0.75em and remove the p p top margin entirely (so only one 0.75em gap between paragraphs).
- Reduce heading margin-top to 0.75em and margin-bottom to 0.3em.
- Keep line-height at 1.65 if the intra-line spacing feels right, or drop it to 1.55 if 1.65 feels a bit loose.
- Add `!important` to our rules so they beat Kilo’s nested 24px heading margins.
- Set first-child headings to margin-top: 0.
- Tighten ul/ol margins and li spacing.

Here’s the updated CSS block:

